he crate-private field formatter `SpanFields`, and no public item is added or changed (packages/escher-telemetry/src/lib.rs:102-116; packages/escher-telemetry/src/format.rs:138-177; packages/escher-telemetry/src/format.rs:200-250; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md). Target allowlist and scrub: the sink admits two public prefix sets, `ENGINE_TARGET_PREFIXES` and `ESCHER_TARGET_PREFIXES` (`escher_`, the underscore part of the prefix) — the fifth public scrub constant, beside `SAFE_FIELDS`, `CONTENT_FIELDS` and `REDACTED`; an event whose target starts with a prefix in `ENGINE_TARGET_PREFIXES` prints only `SAFE_FIELDS`, every other field (`message` included) as `{name}=[redacted]`; an event whose target starts with a prefix in `ESCHER_TARGET_PREFIXES` prints every field not in `CONTENT_FIELDS`, those redacted; an event whose target starts with a prefix of neither set is dropped whole — zero bytes, no time, target or newline — at every level, WARN and ERROR included, and whatever `RUST_LOG` names, a bridged `log` record judged by the target it was logged under (packages/escher-telemetry/src/format.rs:22-111; packages/escher-telemetry/src/format.rs:144-148). Panic event: ERROR at target `escher_telemetry::panic`, fields `panic.file` · `panic.line` · `panic.column` · `panic.payload` (redacted), then the previous hook (packages/escher-telemetry/src/panic.rs:4-24)
