ailure in this order: the verb by exact name (absent → `unknown-verb`; so does a session-level verb or, since 2026-10-12-self-description, the tool-level `help`, refused before its arguments are read, and a verb the table lists in a shape no `Command` has), then the call's arguments in the order passed (a name the verb lacks → `malformed` with `Fault::Unnamed`; a name passed before → `Repeated`), then the verb's arguments in the schema's order (required and absent → `Missing`; a value of another kind → `WrongKind`; a value outside its bound, or a text that is no key name → `OutOfBound`). `Command` is exactly `Snapshot` · `Click { id }` · `Type { id, text }` · `Press { key, shift }` · `Advance { ms: u32 }` · `Scroll { id }` · `Screenshot { id: Option<String> }` (the last since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot), with `spec() -> &'static VerbSpec`; the session-level check is `validate_session(call: &Call) -> Result<SessionCommand, Refusal>` — `validate`'s rules and order over the three session-level rows and, since 2026-10-12-self-description, the tool-level `help`, an instance-level verb reading `unknown-verb` there and an argument to `help` `malformed` with `Fault::Unnamed` — with `SessionCommand` exactly `Start { app }` · `Status` · `Stop` · `Help` and a `spec()` of its own (`Help`'s is `HELP`); `Key` has one variant per name of `KEY_NAMES` (`ALL`, `name`, `from_name`). `Refusal` holds a `Cause` and, only beside `malformed`, a `Fault` (private fields; `new(cause)`, `malformed(fault)`, `cause()`, `fault()`; `Display` as `{name}: {remedy}` or `{name} ({fault}): {remedy}`; `std::error::Error`). `Cause` is closed at eight, listed in `CAUSES` (`[Cause; 8]`, ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18) — `unknown-verb` · `malformed` · `not-found` · `stale` · `disabled` · `covered` · `off-screen` · `fonts-unavailable`, the eighth (meaning "the app this session holds has no font it can paint text with", remedy "boot the app with a font it can decode") — each with a fixed `name()`, `m